event('isfahan','A Safavid civic square',1601,1650,'Early 17th century CE','West Asia','Architecture','Esfahan','UNESCO places Shah Abbas I’s Meidan Emam complex in the early seventeenth century.',unesco(115),'The half-century bounds are an editorial filter band for “early seventeenth century,” not exact project dates.')
event('taj-mahal','A Mughal marble mausoleum',1631,1648,'1631–1648 CE','South Asia','Architecture','Agra','UNESCO dates construction of the Taj Mahal under Shah Jahan to 1631–1648.',unesco(252),'This reproduces the date range in the cited UNESCO account; other works may distinguish building phases.')
events.sort(key=lambda x:(x['start'],x['end'],x['id']))
assert len(events)==24

business=[]
def business_case(id,title,topic,setup,facts,choices,followup,repairs,ref,teaching,report=None):
 first=[dict(label=a,consequence=b,signal=c) for a,b,c in choices]
 final=[dict(label=a,consequence=b,signal=c) for a,b,c in repairs]
 x=dict(id=id,title=title,topic=topic,setup=setup,facts=facts,choices=first,followup=followup,repairs=final,passage=passage(ref),commentaryUrl=comment(ref.split('-')[0]),teaching=teaching,sources=[])
 if report:x['sources'].append(hadith(*report))
 try:x['secondCommentaryUrl']=second('business-qurtubi','ar-qurtubi',ref.split('-')[0])
 except ValueError:pass
 business.append(x)

business_case('hidden-battery','The battery nobody mentioned','Disclosure','You sell a used laptop. It works on a charger, but the battery lasts only ten minutes.',['You know about the battery.','The listing says “works well.”'],[('Describe the battery before taking payment.','The buyer can assess the actual condition.','Source-aligned'),('Wait to see whether the buyer asks.','The buyer may rely on a description you know is incomplete.','Needs repair'),('Pause the sale and test the laptop again.','A second test can clarify the description, provided you do not conceal what is already known.','Clarify first')],'The buyer asks you to put the condition in the receipt.',[('Record the known defect and agreed price.','Both sides keep a clear record of what was disclosed.','Source-aligned'),('Write “sold as seen” and omit the known defect.','A general phrase does not explain the concealed battery condition.','Needs repair')],'4:29','Al-Muyassar explains trade by mutual consent rather than wrongful taking. Applying that principle to this laptop is an editorial exercise.',('bukhari:2079','Hakim ibn Hizam’s report links honest disclosure with blessing in a transaction.'))
business_case('short-weight','The underfilled spice packet','Fair measures','Your 500 g packets contain 470 g. A colleague says the difference is too small to matter.',['The scale was checked.','The label still promises 500 g.'],[('Correct the weight or the label before selling.','The advertised and delivered quantities can agree.','Source-aligned'),('Keep the label because most buyers will not weigh it.','Customers receive less than the stated quantity.','Needs repair'),('Stop sales while checking the affected batch.','You avoid repeating an uncertain measurement.','Clarify first')],'Some underfilled packets have already been sold.',[('Identify the affected sales and offer a clear remedy.','Customers can receive the missing quantity or an agreed correction.','Source-aligned'),('Fix future packets but ignore the earlier shortage.','The earlier customers still bear the known shortfall.','Needs repair')],'83:1-3','Al-Muyassar describes the contrast between demanding full measure and giving others less. The packet and remedy are fictional applications.')
business_case('moving-deadline','The delivery date that changed','Contracts','Your workshop accepted an order due Friday. A larger client now wants the same production slot.',['The first customer agreed to Friday.','No revised date has been accepted.'],[('Keep the agreed slot or seek a genuine revision.','The customer can decide whether a new date is acceptable.','Source-aligned'),('Move the first order and notify them afterward.','You change a material promise without agreement.','Needs repair'),('Check capacity before accepting the second order.','You can avoid making incompatible promises.','Clarify first')],'A delay now seems unavoidable.',[('Explain promptly and discuss a remedy.','The customer can make an informed choice about the delay.','Source-aligned'),('Give repeated reassuring updates without a realistic date.','Reassurance hides the unresolved delivery problem.','Needs repair')],'5:1','Al-Muyassar includes people’s agreements and transactions in its explanation of fulfilling commitments. Contract remedies here are learning suggestions, not rulings.')
business_case('unpaid-work','A completed job and an unpaid invoice','Payment','A freelancer completed the agreed work. Your company can pay but wants to retain cash for another purchase.',['The work met the agreed scope.','The agreed payment is due.'],[('Pay on the agreed terms.','The worker receives the compensation already earned.','Source-aligned'),('Delay because the freelancer is unlikely to complain.','You retain another person’s due payment for your convenience.','Needs repair'),('Check the invoice against the agreement today.','A genuine check can clarify an error without becoming an indefinite delay.','Clarify first')],'The accounts team proposes another month of delay.',[('Resolve any real discrepancy and release the due payment.','A specific accounting issue is separated from avoidance.','Source-aligned'),('Ask the worker to keep waiting without a reason.','The same unpaid obligation continues.','Needs repair')],'16:90','Al-Muyassar describes justice as giving people their due. This case applies that teaching to a fictional completed job.',('bukhari:2270','Abu Hurayra’s report includes taking a worker’s full labor without paying the wage.'))
business_case('debtor-hardship','When a customer genuinely cannot pay','Debt','A customer with an outstanding debt lost their income and explains that they cannot currently repay.',['The debt is acknowledged.','The difficulty is genuine in this fictional case.'],[('Discuss time and an achievable repayment arrangement.','You respond to the stated hardship rather than pretending it does not exist.','Source-aligned'),('Threaten public humiliation to force immediate payment.','Pressure does not create money the customer does not have.','Needs repair'),('Clarify the situation respectfully before agreeing details.','Both sides can understand what is possible.','Clarify first')],'You can afford to forgive part of the debt.',[('Consider remission without turning it into publicity.','You can reduce the debt while preserving the customer’s dignity.','Source-aligned'),('Offer remission only if they post a promotional testimonial.','The proposed help becomes pressure for a marketing benefit.','Needs repair')],'2:280','Al-Muyassar explains giving an insolvent debtor time, and describes remission as better. Practical arrangements in this case are editorial examples.')
business_case('able-to-pay','Delay by a customer who can pay','Debt','Your shop has funds to settle a due supplier invoice, but delaying would improve this month’s cash balance.',['The invoice is due and undisputed.','The shop has enough funds.'],[('Settle the due invoice.','The supplier receives payment according to the agreement.','Source-aligned'),('Delay until the supplier threatens action.','You use avoidable delay as a negotiating tactic.','Needs repair'),('Check the exact due date and amount now.','You can resolve uncertainty before deciding.','Clarify first')],'A colleague confuses this with genuine financial hardship.',[('Distinguish inability from a convenient delay.','The actual facts stay central to the decision.','Source-aligned'),('Claim that every delayed payment is hardship.','The label conceals the shop’s ability to pay.','Needs repair')],'5:1','The commitment reading is paired with a specific report about avoidable delay. Do not equate wealth with freedom from obligations.',('bukhari:2400','Abu Hurayra’s report identifies delay in repayment by an able debtor as injustice.'))
business_case('unclear-loan','The friendly loan with no record','Contracts','Two friends agree on a deferred loan, then remember different amounts and due dates.',['Repayment is deferred.','The amount and date were never recorded.'],[('Agree on a clear written record together.','Both parties can check the same terms.','Source-aligned'),('Treat asking for a record as an insult.','The disagreement remains unresolved.','Needs repair'),('Pause and clarify what each person actually agreed.','You avoid recording an amount one party disputes.','Clarify first')],'A draft contains the wrong amount.',[('Correct it before either person accepts it.','The document reflects the actual agreement.','Source-aligned'),('Leave it because a signature matters more than accuracy.','The record preserves a known error.','Needs repair')],'2:282','Al-Muyassar explains recording a deferred debt to preserve rights and avoid dispute. This short activity does not replace the verse’s full discussion of writing and witnesses.')
business_case('client-deposit','Whose money is the deposit?','Trust','A client leaves funds with you to buy materials for their project. You consider using the money temporarily for your own order.',['The money was entrusted for a stated purchase.','The client has not authorized another use.'],[('Keep the funds for their agreed purpose.','The client’s entrusted money stays available.','Source-aligned'),('Use it and hope to replace it before anyone notices.','You change the use without the owner’s knowledge.','Needs repair'),('Ask about any proposed change before acting.','The owner can accept or refuse with the facts in view.','Clarify first')],'The client requests an account of the spending.',[('Provide an accurate record and return any balance.','The owner can inspect what happened to their funds.','Source-aligned'),('Invent receipts to conceal a temporary diversion.','A false record adds concealment to the original problem.','Needs repair')],'4:58','Al-Muyassar explains returning entrusted things to their owners. The deposit scenario is an editorial application, not a ruling on a real contract.')
business_case('unseen-commission','The recommendation with a hidden incentive','Disclosure','You recommend a supplier as independent advice while receiving a referral fee if the customer chooses them.',['The customer thinks the comparison is independent.','You have a financial incentive.'],[('Explain the incentive before the recommendation.','The customer can evaluate the advice with that fact in view.','Source-aligned'),('Keep the incentive secret because the product is decent.','The customer cannot assess the conflict you know about.','Needs repair'),('Offer a comparison without pretending neutrality.','The recommendation’s basis can be made clear.','Clarify first')],'The supplier asks you to claim there is no commission.',[('Decline the false statement and correct any misleading description.','The customer receives an honest account.','Source-aligned'),('Use the supplier’s wording despite knowing it is false.','The recommendation now includes a direct falsehood.','Needs repair')],'4:29','Al-Muyassar explains lawful trade by consent and rejects wrongful taking. Disclosure of this fictional incentive is applied reasoning beyond the fetched text.',('bukhari:2079','The report stresses truth and disclosure in a transaction; it does not define every modern referral arrangement.'))
business_case('cosmetic-repair','A repair hidden under fresh paint','Disclosure','A cabinet has structural damage. Fresh paint makes it look new in photographs.',['The damage affects use.','The buyer cannot see it in the photos.'],[('Show the damaged area and describe the repair.','The buyer can judge the actual item.','Source-aligned'),('Photograph only the undamaged side.','The presentation conceals a material fact.','Needs repair'),('Have the structure checked before listing it.','You can learn what is safe to claim.','Clarify first')],'The buyer asks whether it is structurally sound.',[('Answer according to the inspection and known limits.','You avoid promising more than the evidence supports.','Source-aligned'),('Say “perfect” to finish the sale.','The answer hides an unresolved defect.','Needs repair')],'4:29','The consent reading provides the wider ethical setting. The cabinet is a modern fictional application.',('muslim:102','Abu Hurayra’s report describes concealed wet food and the need to make its condition visible.'))
business_case('price-surprise','The fee revealed after agreement','Pricing','A customer agrees to a quoted total. At collection, you add a mandatory fee that was already known to you.',['The fee was foreseeable.','The customer relied on the quoted total.'],[('Explain the complete price before agreement.','The customer can decide with the total visible.','Source-aligned'),('Reveal the fee only after the work is finished.','The customer faces a cost they were not able to evaluate.','Needs repair'),('Clarify what the original quote actually included.','You can distinguish a real change in scope from an undisclosed charge.','Clarify first')],'The customer challenges the extra fee.',[('Review the agreement and seek a transparent resolution.','The disputed term can be discussed using the original record.','Source-aligned'),('Insist that small print need never be explained.','The foreseeable misunderstanding remains unresolved.','Needs repair')],'5:1','Al-Muyassar includes transactions in fulfilling agreements. The example addresses clarity, not a universal rule about every pricing structure.')
business_case('false-testimonial','A review from someone who never bought','Truthfulness','A friend offers to post a glowing customer review without buying or using the service.',['No customer experience took place.','Readers will think the review is independent.'],[('Ask for genuine feedback from actual users.','A testimonial can describe a real experience.','Source-aligned'),('Accept the invented review to help the launch.','Readers receive a false account.','Needs repair'),('Invite the friend to test the service and disclose the relationship.','Any later account can state what actually happened.','Clarify first')],'An invented review is already live.',[('Correct or remove the misleading review.','Future readers can avoid relying on a fabricated experience.','Source-aligned'),('Leave it because no one can prove the reviewer was not a customer.','The misleading account remains available.','Needs repair')],'17:36','Al-Muyassar calls for checking what one does not know. Applying that reading to testimonials is editorial reasoning.',('bukhari:6094','The report connects persistent truthfulness with righteousness and warns about lying.'))
assert len(business)==12

readings=[]
def reading(id,title,ref,kind,report,narrator,summary,establishes,limits,teaching,additional=None):
 anchor=ref.split('-')[0]
 sources=[hadith(report,f'Report attributed to {narrator}; original concise paraphrase, not a quotation of the modern English translation.')]
 if additional:sources.append(hadith(*additional))
 readings.append(dict(id=id,title=title,topic=kind,kind=kind,passage=passage(ref),narrator=narrator,reportSummary=summary,establishes=establishes,limits=limits,teaching=teaching,commentaryUrl=comment(anchor),secondCommentaryUrl=second('revelation-ibn-kathir','ar-ibn-kathir',anchor),sources=sources,reliability='The named report is included in Sahih al-Bukhari. This app identifies the collection and narrator; it does not independently regrade chains or assume every surrounding story has the same status.'))
reading('first-reading','The opening of Al-Alaq','96:1-5','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:4953','Aisha','Aisha’s report describes the beginning of revelation at Hira and the first reading instructions.','The report connects these opening instructions with the encounter at Hira.','The report does not provide an exact Gregorian calendar day. It does not say the entire surah was revealed at once.','Al-Muyassar explains these opening verses as instructions to read in the Creator’s name and mentions teaching by the pen.')
reading('safa-warning','A warning at Safa','111:1-5','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:4971','Ibn Abbas','Ibn Abbas describes a public warning at Safa, Abu Lahab’s hostile response and the revelation of the surah’s opening.','The report explicitly connects the opening of Al-Masad with the response at that gathering.','Its narrative connection does not supply an exact CE year. Do not add details about every person present.','Al-Muyassar explains the passage’s warning concerning Abu Lahab and his wife. The complete surah is shown below.')
reading('qiblah','News of a changed direction','2:144','General context','bukhari:399','Al-Bara ibn Azib','Al-Bara describes prayer toward Jerusalem for sixteen or seventeen months, then a change toward the Kaaba and news reaching another congregation.','The report gives the practical setting and reception of the changed direction.','Keep the narrated sixteen-or-seventeen-month uncertainty. This short report is not an exhaustive catalogue of all reports about 2:144.','Al-Muyassar identifies the new direction with Al-Masjid al-Haram in Makkah.')
reading('safa-marwa','Why “no blame” needs context','2:158','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:1643','Urwa reporting Aisha','Aisha corrects Urwa’s inference about omitting the walk. She connects the wording to the Ansar’s earlier association with Manat and their hesitation.','The report explains why an isolated phrase led the questioner to a mistaken conclusion.','Other transmitted accounts emphasize different earlier practices. This selected report does not establish that every individual had identical hesitation.','Al-Muyassar describes Safa and Marwa among the signs of worship and does not read “no blame” as permission to omit the rite.',('bukhari:4495','A longer parallel report includes further discussion with Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman. Read it alongside Aisha’s account.'))
reading('fasting-nights','An earlier restriction and a concession','2:187','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:4508','Al-Bara','Al-Bara connects the concession concerning marital relations on fasting nights with an earlier restriction and people failing to keep it.','The report identifies a circumstance linked to the concession in the verse.','The complete verse also addresses eating, drinking and retreat in mosques. The brief report does not explain every clause by itself.','Al-Muyassar describes the permission at night, the boundary at dawn and the restriction during mosque retreat. This is a contextual reading, not a personalized fasting ruling.')
reading('pilgrimage-trade','Markets during pilgrimage','2:198','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:4519','Ibn Abbas','Ibn Abbas names earlier markets and reports reluctance to trade during pilgrimage, followed by revelation of the relevant wording.','The narration explicitly links the concern about seasonal trade to the verse.','The report addresses that concern; it is not a blanket ruling about every modern transaction during Hajj.','Al-Muyassar explains seeking provision through trade during pilgrimage and remembrance after departing Arafat.')
reading('beloved-garden','A garden given after hearing a verse','3:92','Response after revelation','bukhari:1461','Anas, through Ishaq ibn Abd Allah','Anas describes Abu Talha offering his beloved garden after the verse was revealed and receiving guidance to direct it to relatives.','The narrative demonstrates a response to revelation.','The garden offer follows revelation in the report; it should not be relabeled as the event that caused the verse to be revealed.','Al-Muyassar explains giving from what one loves. The case illustrates a reader’s response to that teaching.')
reading('spilled-drink','Responding when news arrives','5:90','Response after revelation','bukhari:4617','Anas ibn Malik','Anas reports people pouring out their drink when a messenger brought news of its prohibition.','The report describes how news was received and acted upon.','This account does not itself state that this gathering caused 5:90 to be revealed. The exact setting of every stage of prohibition is beyond this short report.','Al-Muyassar includes intoxicants and gambling among the prohibited acts named in the verse.')
reading('slander','The report of the false accusation','24:11-16','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:4141','Aisha','Aisha’s extended account recounts the false accusation, the distress it caused and revelation concerning her innocence.','The report ties the opening of this passage to the accusation and its resolution.','The full report is long and its relationship to particular campaign dates is debated. A precise CE year is not asserted here. The displayed verses are selected context, not the report’s whole revelation passage.','Al-Muyassar identifies Aisha as the subject of the false accusation and explains the warning about passing on speech without knowledge.')
reading('raised-voices','Voices in the presence of the Prophet','49:2','Transmitted occasion','bukhari:4845','Ibn Abi Mulaika, with a report from Ibn al-Zubayr','The narration describes Abu Bakr and Umar disagreeing about a recommendation when a Banu Tamim delegation arrived, their voices rising and revelation of the verse.','The report explicitly connects that exchange with the instruction about raised voices.','A sub-narrator does not remember one recommended person’s name. Preserve that uncertainty rather than filling it from another account without attribution.','Al-Muyassar explains the special respect due in addressing the Prophet. This is not a license to transfer every detail to an unrelated modern dispute.')
assert len(readings)==10

packs=[]
def pack(id,title,age,topic,minutes,prompt,answer,distractors,explain,discussion,activity,close,ref=None,report=None,teaching=''):
 options=[answer]+distractors
 # Fixed rotation spreads correct-answer positions without random runtime behavior.
 shift=len(packs)%len(options);options=options[shift:]+options[:shift]
 x=dict(id=id,title=title,age=age,topic=topic,minutes=minutes,question=prompt,options=options,answer=options.index(answer),explanation=explain,discussion=discussion,activity=activity,close=close,teaching=teaching,sources=[])
 if ref:x.update(passage=passage(ref),commentaryUrl=comment(ref.split('-')[0]))
 if report:x['sources'].append(hadith(*report))
 packs.append(x)
pack('names-that-care','Names that care','5–7','Kindness',10,'What does the reading warn against?','Mocking others and using hurtful nicknames.',['Learning someone’s chosen name.','Speaking gently.'],'The selected passage names ridicule and offensive nicknames.','How could a nickname feel funny to one person and hurtful to another? Use made-up examples, without naming someone who was hurt.','Each person invents a kind greeting for a fictional new neighbor. Everyone may pass if they prefer.','Choose one greeting to try together. Do not record names or personal stories.','49:11',teaching='Al-Muyassar explains the warnings about ridicule, fault-finding and disliked names. The greeting exercise is an editorial application.')
